1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,219
My Turn to Choose.

3
00:00:03,219 --> 00:00:05,719
Emma comes over on Saturday afternoon.

4
00:00:05,719 --> 00:00:08,052
I have a board game ready on the table.

5
00:00:08,052 --> 00:00:09,729
She has brought a ball.

6
00:00:09,729 --> 00:00:13,000
We look at each other's plans without saying anything for a moment.

7
00:00:13,226 --> 00:00:14,572
What are you in the mood for?

8
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:16,114
This game.

9
00:00:16,114 --> 00:00:18,260
I've been waiting all week to play it.

10
00:00:18,482 --> 00:00:20,244
I was hoping we could go outside.

11
00:00:20,244 --> 00:00:21,849
It's finally stopped raining.

12
00:00:22,132 --> 00:00:25,782
Neither of us wants to sound difficult, so we both say whatever you want.

13
00:00:25,782 --> 00:00:27,522
That doesn't help at all.

14
00:00:27,522 --> 00:00:29,532
Then Emma looks at the clock.

15
00:00:29,762 --> 00:00:31,108
How about we do both?

16
00:00:31,108 --> 00:00:33,816
Half an hour outside, then we come in for the game.

17
00:00:34,084 --> 00:00:35,411
That works.

18
00:00:35,411 --> 00:00:38,859
We tell Mom where we're going and walk to the little court near my house.

19
00:00:38,859 --> 00:00:42,296
Emma shows me a passing game that doesn't involve keeping score.

20
00:00:42,296 --> 00:00:45,307
Soon, I'm having too much fun to watch the time.

21
00:00:45,530 --> 00:00:46,647
Half an hour's up.

22
00:00:46,647 --> 00:00:47,886
Ready to head back?

23
00:00:48,172 --> 00:00:49,280
Already?

24
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:50,468
Okay.

25
00:00:50,468 --> 00:00:52,197
A deal is a deal.

26
00:00:52,197 --> 00:00:55,312
Back at home, we get water and sit down at the table.

27
00:00:55,312 --> 00:00:59,312
I explain the rules, and Emma asks a few questions before we start.

28
00:00:59,522 --> 00:01:00,889
It's your turn to choose.

29
00:01:00,889 --> 00:01:02,212
Which piece do you want?

30
00:01:02,476 --> 00:01:03,813
The blue one.

31
00:01:03,813 --> 00:01:05,511
Always the blue one.

32
00:01:05,511 --> 00:01:08,293
Emma takes the green piece, and we begin.

33
00:01:08,293 --> 00:01:12,157
By the end of the afternoon, we've both tried something the other person wanted.

34
00:01:12,157 --> 00:01:14,938
We still disagree about which activity was better.

35
00:01:14,938 --> 00:01:17,855
Fortunately, nobody needs to win that argument.
